including elements, modules, and systems serving primarily industrial wastewater and energy markets, municipal and desalination applications, and life sciences and specialty sectors. It also offers AMBERLITE ion exchange resins, FILMTEC reverse osmosis and nanofiltration elements, and INGE and ITEGRATEC ultrafiltration modules. In addition, the company offers engineered products and integrated solutions for the non-residential, residential, and repair-and-remodel construction markets, includes TYVEK house wrap, STYROFOAM insulation, and CORIAN solid surface. Further, it engages in the design and production of engineered components, systems, and process solutions used in OEM and operational applications, such as automotive, aerospace, printing, and packaging. Additionally, the company offers Vespel shapes and parts, MOLYKOTE specialty lubricants, BETAFORCE and BETASEAL structural adhesives, and Cyrel flexographic printing plates. The company was formerly known as DowDuPont Inc. and changed its name to DuPont de Nemours, Inc. in June 2019. DuPont de Nemours, Inc. was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Wilmington, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lori D. Koch | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $457K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers, with revenue falling 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["DuPont de Nemours, Inc. is a large-cap basic materials business with a $20.4B market cap on $6.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -19% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $227M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 80% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8007368049423812},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $14.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["53 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How New Water Filtration And AI R&D Tools Will Impact DuPont (DD) Investors","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-dd/dupont-de-nemours/news/how-new-water-filtration-and-ai-rd-tools-will-impact-dupont","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794583672.52,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DuPont de Nemours (NYSE:DD) Sets New 1-Year High \u2013 Still a Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/dupont-de-nemours-nysedd-sets-new-1-year-high-still-a-buy.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794570521.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DuPont (DD): Semiconductor Water Demand Offers Growth Amid Middle East Delays","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dupont-dd-semiconductor-water-demand-192512626.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794511512.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DuPont (DD) Unveils High Flow Water Purification Modules For Chip And Industrial Use","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-dd/dupont-de-nemours/news/dupont-dd-unveils-high-flow-water-purification-modules-for-c","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794493553.285,"origin":"tiingo","sentime